      "id": "acceptor-coupling/components/l1h12-mean-ablation",
      "title": "L1H12 contributes under within-example mean ablation",
      "summary": "On the 500-row, 304-gene held-out-within-validation target, within-example token-mean ablation of L1H12 produced a selective masked-acceptor-margin component pattern and passed the frozen seven-path decision rule (Holm-adjusted p = 0.00175).",
      "record_kind": "finding",
      "status": "supported",
      "evidence_rung": "output-ov",
      "review_tier": "confirmatory",
      "claim_eligible": true,
      "scope": "A component-level response to one head-output intervention at the masked acceptor G in validation chromosomes chr11, chr16, and chr19.",
      "first_missing_bridge": "No edge or path intervention establishes what L1H12 writes, whether it mediates donor information, or where that information is delivered.",
